hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16528","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Atik, one of Banu Salimah, from his father Abdullah ibn Atik, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever goes out from his house striving in the cause of Allah Almighty, then he said with these three fingers of his, the middle, the index, and the thumb, and he joined them, and he said: And where are the strivers, then he falls from his mount and dies, then his reward has fallen upon Allah Almighty, or his mount stings him and he dies, then his reward has fallen upon Allah, or he dies a natural death, then his reward has fallen upon Allah Almighty, and by Allah, indeed it is a word I never heard from any Arab before the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then he dies, then his reward has fallen upon Allah Almighty, and whoever dies suddenly has deserved the final return."
